# Migration Rules

- Follow `/docs/data-model` and `/docs/database/29-migration-implementation.md`.
- MySQL is the target database.
- UUID is the approved primary key format.
- Money uses decimal/numeric, never floating point.
- Every migration MUST have a coherent `down()` method when technically possible.
- Foreign keys MUST respect migration order.
- Critical invariants MUST be represented by constraints/indexes where possible.
- Do not put business workflows into migrations.
- Never store secrets in seeders or migrations.
